<title>USA: U.S. cash soymeal - Rail, truck basis offers slip.</title>
<headline>U.S. cash soymeal - Rail, truck basis offers slip.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rail and truck offers in some soymeal markets were lower Tuesday in response to lackluster demand from buyers, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The prices are just too high, but I think they are due for a correction, said one southeastern soymeal merchant.</p>
<p>Cash dealers said that the market is beginning to show signs of weakness in both the nearby and forward contracts as the week wears on.</p>
<p>Soymeal export sales have started to lag behind shipments and many expect U.S. exports to slow significantly as the South American crop is marketed in March.</p>
<p>&quot;As we move into March, the crush is going to have to button up (slow down) to offset the exports and meet just domestic demand,&quot; an Indiana dealer said.</p>
